  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `screenshot.png` (the maintainer's app screenshot, 1512 x 1199) is added at the repo root.\n- `README.md`: one Markdown image line, placed after the title and the opening description and before `## What it does`. Alt text describes the window: model browser left, 3D viewport with a block on a vise, WCS (G54) properties panel right.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `.gitignore` line 48 is `/*.png`, which ignores root PNGs, so the file was added with `git add -f`. `.gitignore` is not edited. The file is tracked and renders on GitHub via its relative path.\n- Docs-only: no build or gate was run, as the issue calls for. Only `README.md` and the PNG changed; no snapshot PNG was touched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --stat origin/main`: `README.md` (+2 lines) and `screenshot.png` (new).\n- The branch has two commits with the same subject: the first adds the PNG, the second adds the README line. Both end with `Fixes #1276`.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1276\n",
